# Geodesic thorn testsuite configuration.
#
# Seven tests.  The first four integrate one particle on a prograde
# equatorial circular orbit (r = 11.989, M = 2, a = 0.5, 32 Cactus
# steps of 100 coordinate-time units; Exact = yes except
# circ_orbit_grid); the next two are a 100-particle pair on a ring of
# the same circular orbits (particle i at angle 2*pi*i/100),
# Exact = no, with and without AMR; the last is a 200-particle bound
# equatorial elliptic orbit under 3-level AMR:
#
#   circ_orbit           compares the full particle state dump
#                        (t x y z u^t u^x u^y u^z tau) against the
#                        reference data row by row; any change of the
#                        trajectory fails the test.
#
#   circ_orbit_conserved runs the same dump through util/check_conserved,
#                        which prints the Kerr constants of motion
#                        (E, L_z) for every row, and compares those two
#                        columns against the reference; a broken
#                        integrator shows up as a drift of E / L_z.
#
#   circ_orbit_mpi       the same run with 2 MPI ranks.  Only rank 0
#                        integrates the particles (the in-code rank-0
#                        policy; in Exact mode the local safe-region
#                        checks are skipped so the particle is never
#                        falsely dropped by its own rank's local
#                        patch), so the dump must be bit-identical to
#                        the single-rank reference.
#
#   circ_orbit_grid      the same orbit with Exact = no: the metric
#                        and Christoffel symbols come from the ADMBase
#                        grid (KerrSchild initial data in 3+1 form)
#                        via polynomial interpolation + 6th-order FD
#                        derivatives, with the past time levels filled
#                        by Carpet (Carpet::init_fill_timelevels = yes)
#                        so the stationary-metric detection engages
#                        (d_t g = 0).  Validates the whole grid-sampling
#                        pipeline; the trajectory deviates slightly
#                        from the analytic one (grid discretization)
#                        but the dump must be reproducible.
#
#   circ_orbit_amr       100 particles on a ring of the circular
#                        orbits above, Exact = no, with AMR: two
#                        static refinement boxes centred on the origin
#                        (half-widths 16 and 8, refinement factor 2,
#                        on a 50^3 base grid of dx = 1), so every
#                        particle (the orbit stays at r in
#                        [11.7, 12.1]) lives on the level-1 grid
#                        (dx = 0.5) for the whole run and the
#                        level-2 box (dx = 0.25) is never sampled.  Single process: with Exact = no the
#                        refinement patches must be symmetric about
#                        the origin and only rank 0 integrates, which
#                        breaks under domain decomposition.
#
#   circ_orbit_100       control run for circ_orbit_amr: the same
#                        100 particles on the same 50^3 grid with no
#                        refinement, so the AMR test's dump can be
#                        compared against a known-good coarser-grid
#                        run (E / L_z scatter from check_conserved is
#                        ~3x smaller on the refined grid, consistent
#                        with the 2nd-order 27-point metric
#                        interpolation).
#
#   ellipse_orbit_amr    200 particles on one bound equatorial
#                        elliptic geodesic (Kerr M = 2, a = 0.5,
#                        Kerr-Schild coordinates): pericentre Rp = 7.5,
#                        apocentre (64, 0, 0), E = 0.9742480384407799,
#                        L_z = 7.1053558433047188; particle i at
#                        azimuth 2*pi*i/200 of the first winding of the
#                        strongly precessing orbit (~4.02 pi per radial
#                        period).  Exact = yes (built-in analytic
#                        Kerr-Schild metric, sexact branch) on a 144^3
#                        base grid (domain +-72, dx = 1) with a static
#                        3-level spherical refinement (boxes 36/18/9,
#                        refinement factor 2), so the particles occupy
#                        all four levels at t = 0 and cross level
#                        boundaries in both directions as the orbit
#                        runs through ~2.42 radial periods
#                        (t to 3300).  Exact =
#                        yes is deliberate: the 2nd-order grid metric
#                        (Exact = no) corrupts the constants of motion
#                        of this strongly eccentric orbit (init u^t
#                        re-solve + coherent integration error push
#                        the near-pericentre particles across the
#                        plunge boundary Rp* = 7.35); with the exact
#                        metric E and L_z are conserved to integrator
#                        precision and all 200 particles survive.
#                        Validates the per-level AMR pipeline
#                        (acquire, pick_level, 4:1 subcycling on three
#                        layers) and the particle integrator on an
#                        eccentric orbit; the grid-metric path itself
#                        is covered by circ_orbit_grid / circ_orbit_amr.
#
# The reference files (test/circ_orbit/geodesic_particles.txt,
# test/circ_orbit_conserved/geodesic_particles.txt,
# test/circ_orbit_mpi/geodesic_particles.txt,
# test/circ_orbit_grid/geodesic_particles.txt,
# test/circ_orbit_amr/geodesic_particles.txt,
# test/circ_orbit_100/geodesic_particles.txt and
# test/ellipse_orbit_amr/geodesic_particles.txt) are the raw dumps of
# verified runs.

EXTENSIONS txt

TEST circ_orbit
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST circ_orbit_conserved
{
  POSTPROC check_conserved
  RELTOL 1e-8
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST circ_orbit_mpi
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 2
}

TEST circ_orbit_grid
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST circ_orbit_amr
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST circ_orbit_100
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 1
}

TEST ellipse_orbit_amr
{
  RELTOL 1e-12
  NPROCS 1
}
